/**
 * Self-boot bootstrap core (conformance G.7–G.9).
 *
 *
 * "Load the .html and it just works": a world HTML that includes ONE boot line
 * (`<script type="module" src="…/webverse-boot.js">`) self-initializes the
 * runtime when opened directly in a browser — no app shell, no query params.
 * Each world is a real web page at a real URL (which is what makes
 * browser-native navigation between worlds exact).
 *
 * A SECOND consumer of the embeddable runtime: this module REUSES
 * `createEngine` (engine/bootstrap), `createWorldSession` (scene/worldSession),
 * `createFeedbackSurface` (feedback), the `NavigationController` (navigation)
 * and `portalInteraction` (interaction) seams, input/controller/render-loop —
 * it does NOT rebuild any of them. `src/main.ts` is the OTHER consumer (the app
 * index); the two mirror the boot shape deliberately (the "second consumer"
 * cost) rather than sharing a function (which would couple main.ts to this).
 *
 * THE CRUX — the hard-constraint-preserving INLINE self-parse (G.4/G.7):
 * the `veml-*` markup lives in the LIVE document the browser loaded, but the
 * HTML dialect's constraint is to parse INERT TEXT, never a DOM-coupled scene
 * graph. So the boot serializes the running document to an HTML STRING
 * (`document.documentElement.outerHTML`) and feeds THAT to the HTML dialect's
 * inert `parseVemlHtml` → `VemlDocument` → the existing build. The live
 * `veml-*` elements stay inert unknown-elements the browser renders as nothing;
 * we read the document's own source ONCE as text and never sync/attach/register
 * custom elements. This is the SAME one-way parse as the XML/URL path. The
 * security property carries: serializing + inert-reparsing runs NO
 * page script a second time — `DOMParser('text/html')` never executes `<script>`
 * content, and the boot script already ran once as the page's real module
 * script.
 *
 * This module exports pure helpers + `runSelfBoot`; it NEVER auto-runs (so it
 * is unit-testable in jsdom). `src/boot/selfBoot.ts` is the tiny Vite entry
 * that invokes `runSelfBoot(document, window)`.
 */
