/**
 * Script Entity/World/Camera host (the entity surface and world navigation of
 * the script API). THE ONLY BABYLON-TOUCHING LAYER of the scene-mutating World
 * API. STATICALLY imported by `worldSession`: it reuses ONLY main-
 * bundle scene factories (`createPrimitiveMesh`/`createLightEntity`/`applyVeml-
 * Transform`/`fetchAssetBytes`/`reservedParams`), so its marginal first-paint
 * cost is ~1.8 KB of its own glue — cheaper AND flatter than a second dynamic
 * import, which perturbs Rolldown's chunking (about +7.2 KB of framing
 * overhead). The prelude WRAPPERS + the `__entity*` host BRIDGES still
 * ride the CODE-SPLIT sandbox chunk — a SCRIPTLESS world still never fetches
 * QuickJS or the wrappers.
 *
 * `createScriptEntityApi(deps)` returns an `EntityApiHost` (src/sandbox/sandbox-
 * Types.ts) bound to ONE freshly-built world: its `scene`, `registry`, `camera`,
 * `controller`, world `worldUrl`, and a `navigate` seam. The Entity/World/Camera
 * host BRIDGES in `sandboxCore.ts` forward to it — `sandboxCore` stays Babylon-
 * free; the boundary is serializable-only.
 *
 * THE HANDLE-AS-ID INVARIANT: every method takes/
 * returns ENTITY-ID STRINGS + plain `{x,y,z}`/`{x,y,z,w}`/`{r,g,b,a}` objects +
 * booleans — NEVER a live Babylon node. A script's Entity handle is a sandbox-
 * side wrapper over an id; the host looks the id up in the FLAT `entityRegistry`
 * and operates on the real node. A forged/stale/foreign id → sane `null`/`false`,
 * never a crash or a cross-world reach (deny-by-default; a fresh host per world).
 *
 * FACTORY REUSE: `createEntity` reuses the SAME
 * scene factories `buildWorld` uses (`createPrimitiveMesh`/`createLightEntity`/
 * the glb path/`applyVemlTransform`/`registry.register`) so a script-created
 * entity is REGISTRY-IDENTICAL to a VEML-parsed one — same registry, walkable/
 * pickable/disposable on the same paths. It mints a hollow handle synchronously
 * (id now), spawns the entity HIDDEN (`setEnabled(false)` — the spawn-hidden
 * contract: a script shows it when ready), and fires `onLoaded` on a SUBSEQUENT tick.
 *
 * ENTITY-TREE-ON-DEMAND: `getParent`/`getChildren` DERIVE from the flat
 * registry + the one-way scene graph (`registry.findByRootNode`/`children`) — NO
 * synced second tree to drift. `setParent` reparents the live node with
 * Babylon `setParent` (WORLD-transform-preserving).
 *
 * Copyright (c) 2019-2026 Five Squared Interactive. All rights reserved.
 */
