/**
 * VEML scene construction.
 *
 * Consumes the typed document model ONE-WAY (no live second tree;
 * src/veml/** stays zero-Babylon — the dependency points this way only).
 * Builds the renderable tier: `container`, `mesh` (glb via mesh-resource),
 * the 11 primitives, lights, audio, and the world-space UI tier
 * (`canvas`/`text`/`image`/`button`, uiEntity.ts). Every built entity becomes
 * an EntityRegistry entry (UUID + tag) owning its Babylon resources, parented
 * per document nesting. The 9 degrade-tier + genuinely-unknown types are
 * classified into the capability registry and skipped.
 *
 * Build rules:
 * - `tag` is REQUIRED for every buildable entity — a missing tag skips the
 *   entity and its whole SUBTREE with a warning (children are never built
 *   detached from their parent).
 * - Containers validate their transform BEFORE creation: anything but a
 *   scaletransform skips the entity. Mesh and primitive entities apply their
 *   transform AFTER load with the result IGNORED — an invalid transform warns
 *   and leaves the default, the entity is kept.
 * - The glb loads from the FIRST `mesh-resource` entry (the document model
 *   resolves those URLs); `mesh-name` is not required, and extra resource
 *   entries warn (multi-file glTF is not loaded).
 * - A failed glb download registers the entity ERRORED with its asset URL,
 *   emits `asset-failed`, and the world keeps loading — one bad asset never
 *   blocks the world, and the failure stays visible in the registry.
 */
